-- title:
--   Galois-invariance of the cusp ∞ on X₀(N)_{ℚ̄}
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and an automorphism $\tau$ of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ as a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra, i.e. an element of $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$. Write $F_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ j_q$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and $\bar{F}_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the elements of $F_N$. The element `arithmeticGalois` $F_N$ $\tau$ is the semilinear automorphism given by the pair consisting of the coefficientwise action of $\tau$ on $\bar{F}_N$ and $\tau$ itself on $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of the subgroup of $\mathrm{RingAut}\ \bar{F}_N \times \mathrm{RingAut}\ \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ of pairs commuting with the structure map). The assertion is that this semilinear automorphism fixes the place `cuspInftyBar N` of $\bar{F}_N$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ — the place whose valuation subring is $\mathrm{qIntegersBar}$, the elements of $q$-order $\geq 0$, constructed from the witness that the coefficientwise image of $j_q$ has $q$-order $-1$ — for the induced action on places.
--
--   This is the statement that the cusp $\infty$ of the modular curve attached to $F_N$ is rational over $\mathbb{Q}$: as a place of the geometric function field $\bar{F}_N$ it is invariant under the arithmetic (coefficientwise) action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$. It is used in the constructions of Galois-stable representatives and height estimates on divisor classes, where the cusp serves as a Galois-invariant base point.
